 (delivery-scope . "Repaired re-delivery of the blocked v1.00.30 W4 guarded compiled-root activation (issue #9690) on top of main fc1a6fa36206accff81abb0b9be07a5be72bc9d2 through the hardened v1.00.31 machinery: one guarded whole-checkout producer invocation in .github/actions/prepare-racket-environment/action.yml that the reviewed CLI executes verbatim and tests/test-compiled-root-workflow.rkt extracts and executes (with unknown-switch and missing-argument failure shapes), published inside the already-contracted q-compiled/ prefix with no allowlist widening; ci.yml's fast-env producer passes the compiled-root input and the fast test shards opt into resolution with compiled-root-mode, while every other prepared-env consumer stays full eager; the restore action exposes q-compiled/trusted-root read-only and setup-racket's pre-resolution step is gated on an explicit resolution mode and runs with or without --module; scripts/ci/compiled-root.rkt keeps --module repeatable, keeps whole-checkout --out mutually exclusive with --module/--final-dir and performs resolution/verification/mapping without a module; activation.json and rollback-drill.json are re-derived at the repaired head with agreeing drill timings (472/481/480 ms) and every recorded head naming a commit that carries the recorded content; the drill harness, its transcript, the red-first review captures and the all-green declared Verify chain (157 tests, arch 32/32, security 64/64, workflows 33/33, check-deps, metrics --lint, fast 1208/1208) are retained under raw/ and bound by SHA256SUMS; the W2 dag-checkpoint re-stamps prepare_action_sha256 = 49bbb6795241550d973f70d12b9e568feb67f8065852c470ff9d8f1a204e683e and setup_action_sha256 = 4873bec295c1bc47964f71304e027ece91a5a003b1db6dcdb477c87ebec51fb0 with its checkpoint hash re-recorded; the lane wiring was re-stamped after round-3 review: the pre-resolution step uses a hyphen-free shell variable, 'auto' is an accepted resolution mode in both CLIs, the fast-shard launch step exports the lane switch, the restore action excludes q-compiled/trusted-root from checkout materialization, and the W2 checkpoint pins were re-stamped for the changed setup action; the lane wiring was re-stamped again after round-4 review, which wired the frozen-doc W4 telemetry (producer cost, restore cost, usable-root hit, bounded eager-fallback compile, compiled-code source), made the one bounded eager gate also run on the off lane so a rollback never lazily compiles, and moved the compiled-root map upload after the shard so the launcher's usable-root telemetry is captured; the declared recovery artifacts were re-derived by re-running the retained drill harness against the committed CLI at the repaired code head ba35b090f78f00cc287133f2b77792fa836919cd (all five phases pass; the retained transcript is the single source of truth for the 472/481/480 ms fallback timings) and are carried forward to the implementation head recorded here; and the report docs/reports/COMPILED-ROOT-ACTIVATION-v1.00.30.md carries the repair note at implementation head c6254a66ca6967d43ad81524ed3ea784f0775fec with content digest 8902bbb6b7adfd5aeb94c71e7280c80dd0bb53aa717606c163115e6283be841c."))